                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A strong habitual desire or fancy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "206ddabd-3927-3174-861b-946db2a7a503",
                                        "entry_id": "041f6c23-8ab9-3ff4-bacb-4222286ce226",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A temporary passion or infatuation, as for some new amusement, pursuit, or fashion; a fad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d13651db-ca13-408f-8a85-56cae8258bb4",
                                                "sense_id": "206ddabd-3927-3174-861b-946db2a7a503",
                                                "text": "Winemaking was a huge craze in the 1970s, when affordable package holidays to the continent gave people a taste for winedrinking, but the recession made it hard to afford off-license prices back home."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c51f692c-2647-3c3d-8e84-1cf87c64680c",
                                        "entry_id": "041f6c23-8ab9-3ff4-bacb-4222286ce226",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crack in the glaze or enamel caused by exposure of the pottery to great or irregular heat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2b38bd1-3262-3652-b2dd-98ca6a377380",
                                        "entry_id": "041f6c23-8ab9-3ff4-bacb-4222286ce226",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Craziness; insanity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0529f5e6-6928-4889-ab2f-9d25f49586e0",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b38bd1-3262-3652-b2dd-98ca6a377380",
                                                "text": "‘A poor fellow with a craze, sir,’ said Mr. Dick, ‘a simpleton, a weak-minded person […] may do what wonderful people may not do. […]’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "craze",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fe0bbbb-c814-3a2c-afda-ef8f7888bfca",
                                        "entry_id": "06097861-cb30-3b4e-a0ba-45eec02306d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To weaken; to impair; to render decrepit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6f39664-8a3f-42d3-aa98-e3fa7dab32c9",
                                                "sense_id": "2fe0bbbb-c814-3a2c-afda-ef8f7888bfca",
                                                "text": "till length of years / And ſedentary numneſs craze my limbs"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "02cc383f-7682-340b-806b-76903e588491",
                                        "entry_id": "06097861-cb30-3b4e-a0ba-45eec02306d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To derange the intellect of; to render insane."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95fdfd70-b5f9-4a53-9a8b-e369b9f8adb5",
                                                "sense_id": "02cc383f-7682-340b-806b-76903e588491",
                                                "text": "any man […] that is crazed and out of his wits"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6aecba0-6e0b-4696-a9d1-a635249ddbd7",
                                                "sense_id": "02cc383f-7682-340b-806b-76903e588491",
                                                "text": "Grief hath crazed my wits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48ff426a-6195-3d00-8157-19ec6d5ac0c5",
                                        "entry_id": "06097861-cb30-3b4e-a0ba-45eec02306d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be crazed, or to act or appear as one that is crazed; to rave; to become insane."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f57a0ca-b9b9-414f-92b3-72bf7a04df8e",
                                                "sense_id": "48ff426a-6195-3d00-8157-19ec6d5ac0c5",
                                                "text": "And if Robin should be cast / Sudden from his turfed grave, / And if Marian should have / Once again her forest days, / She would weep and he would craze: [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "865eb0c5-ab84-378b-a1d6-de0eaa426a7f",
                                        "entry_id": "06097861-cb30-3b4e-a0ba-45eec02306d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To break into pieces; to crush; to grind to powder. See crase."
